course: dictionary
lesson: 3292
title: Est: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «est» has several jobs, and the place where you find it tells you which one it has. In French, «il est content» means «he is happy», so «est» means «is», just like the English word «is».
explain: On a shop front, «Est.» with a full stop is short for «established», which means the business began in that year. In maths or science, «est.» means «estimated», a sensible guess that is close to the real answer. The full stop is your clue that it is a short form.
explain: In English, the ending «-est» means «the most», as in «tallest» and «fastest». Always check the context: a sign, a sum, a French sentence or a comparison will show you which meaning fits.
fact: «Est» means «is» in French: «il est content» means «he is happy».
fact: «Est.» with a full stop is short for «established» (when a shop or school began) or «estimated» (a guess that is close).
fact: «EST» in capitals means Eastern Standard Time, the clock time in the eastern USA and Canada.
fact: The ending «-est» makes superlatives, which mean the most: «big, bigger, biggest»; «tallest», «fastest».
exercise: In a French lesson you read «Il est content.» What does «est» mean? | *is | happy | ends | eats
exercise: A shop sign says «Est. 1902». What does «Est.» mean here? | *Established, so the shop began in 1902 | Eastern Standard Time | Estimated, a guess | Eaten by 1902
exercise: Which ending means the most? | -ing | -er | *-est | -ly
test: In a maths lesson you see «est. 40 sweets». What does est. mean? | Eastern Standard Time | *Estimated, a close guess | Every sweet | Established, the year a shop began
test: Which word uses the ending -est to mean the most? | *tallest | big | jumped | quickly
exam: Ayo sees «EST» on a timetable. What does it show? | *Eastern Standard Time, the clock time in the eastern USA and Canada | Estimated, a close guess | The east side of town | Established, when a school began
